# Intellia360 - Milestone 1: Project Analysis & Technical Blueprint

> **Role**: Lead Frontend Architect  
> **Target Scope**: Student Module & Teacher Module  
> **Phase**: Frontend Development Only  
> **Tech Stack**: Next.js 15, React, TypeScript, Plain CSS (No Tailwind)  
> **Status**: Completed Analysis — Awaiting Approval  

---

## 📌 Executive Architectural Summary

Intellia360 is an AI-powered, gamified Learning Management System (LMS) designed for K-10 students, with an initial focus on Grade 1–10 Math curriculum. The current phase is strictly focused on **Frontend Development** for the **Student Module** and **Teacher Module**, built with **Next.js 15**, **React**, **TypeScript**, and **Plain CSS**. No backend API, authentication system, or database setup will be initialized in this phase.

All UI components and layouts are designed to match the provided reference designs with pixel precision, incorporating smooth responsive behavior, structured CSS architecture, and mock JSON data models.

---

## 1. PRD Analysis Summary

- **Product Vision**: Transition Intellia360 from a plugin-based WordPress/LearnPress LMS into a high-performance, SaaS LMS with native gamification and AI tutoring.
- **Core User Personas (Current Scope Focus)**:
  - **Student (Grades 1–10)**: Engages with gamified missions, video lessons, EduNotes, practice challenges, character collections, and real-time AI Tutor assistance.
  - **Teacher**: Manages classes, tracks student progress & at-risk alerts, assigns worksheets, and uses AI Lesson Planning tools.
- **Core Learning Loop**: Lesson → XP & Gems Earned → Badges & Missions Unlocked → Leaderboard Ranking → Avatar Rewards.
- **Key Functional Requirements**:
  - `FR-STU-1` to `FR-STU-4`: Student today's adventure mission, continue-learning shortcut, XP & streak stats, quest map curriculum browser, AI Tutor / AI Hint integrations.
  - `FR-TCH-1` to `FR-TCH-3`: Class-level completion analytics, worksheet creation/assignment, AI Lesson Planner.
  - `FR-GAM-1` to `FR-GAM-5`: XP, Coins/Gems, Badges, Leaderboard, Daily Streaks, Daily/Weekly Missions.
- **Non-Functional Requirements**: Core pages load in under 2 seconds, responsive design across Desktop (1440px+), Tablet (768px - 1024px), and Mobile (375px - 430px), child-friendly aesthetic.

---

## 2. TRD Analysis Summary

- **Architecture Boundary**: Pure client-side Next.js 15 frontend architecture driven by mock JSON data structures.
- **Frontend Core Stack**:
  - Framework: **Next.js 15** (App Router)
  - UI Library: **React 19**
  - Language: **TypeScript** (Strict mode)
  - Styling: **Plain CSS** with modular page-level stylesheets and custom CSS variables (No Tailwind CSS).
- **Data Flow Strategy**: All state, user stats, quest maps, quiz questions, and leaderboard rankings are powered by static mock JSON modules located in `src/data/`.
- **Modularity Requirement**: Feature-focused React components, isolated CSS files, strict TypeScript interfaces, reusable layout shells (`StudentLayout` and `TeacherLayout`).

